acrn_vm_ram_map() derives an int page count from the user-supplied length.

It does this before validating the full userspace range.

Very large lengths can truncate the page count.

Unaligned lengths can also make the PFNMAP path validate too few pages.

The full length is passed to the hypervisor later.

Reject unaligned ranges and overflowing VA ranges.

Also reject page counts that do not fit the pinning and vmap helpers.

